{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().run();\n    }\n\n    private void run() {\n        try (Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n             PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out, StandardCharsets.UTF_8)))) {\n            \n            int a = sc.nextInt();\n            int b = sc.nextInt();\n            int l = sc.nextInt() - 1;\n            int r = sc.nextInt() - 1;\n\n            int minUnique = 26;\n\n            for (char p = 'a'; p <= 'z'; p++) {\n                for (char q = (char) ('a' + a); q <= 'z'; q++) {\n                    String pattern = buildPattern(a, b, p, q);\n                    int uniqueCount = countUniqueInRange(pattern, l, r);\n                    minUnique = Math.min(minUnique, uniqueCount);\n                }\n            }\n\n            pw.println(minUnique);\n        }\n    }\n\n    private String buildPattern(int a, int b, char p, char q) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) sb.append((char) ('a' + i));\n        for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) sb.append(p);\n        \n        outer:\n        for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) {\n            boolean[] seen = new boolean[26];\n            for (int j = b; j < b + a + i; j++) {\n                if (j < sb.length()) {\n                    seen[sb.charAt(j) - 'a'] = true;\n                }\n            }\n            for (int j = 0; j < 26; j++) {\n                if (!seen[j]) {\n                    sb.append((char) ('a' + j));\n                    continue outer;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) sb.append(q);\n        return sb.toString();\n    }\n\n    private int countUniqueInRange(String pattern, int l, int r) {\n        boolean[] seen = new boolean[26];\n        int len = pattern.length();\n        if (r - l + 1 >= 100_000) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n                seen[pattern.charAt(i) - 'a'] = true;\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int i = l; i <= r; i++) {\n                seen[pattern.charAt(i % len) - 'a'] = true;\n            }\n        }\n        int count = 0;\n        for (boolean b : seen) if (b) count++;\n        return count;\n    }\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstring buildPattern(int a, int b, char p, char q) {\n    string sb;\n    for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) sb += (char)('a' + i);\n    for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) sb += p;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < a; i++) {\n        vector<bool> seen(26, false);\n        for (int j = b; j < b + a + i; j++) {\n            if (j < (int)sb.length()) {\n                seen[sb[j] - 'a'] = true;\n            }\n        }\n        for (int j = 0; j < 26; j++) {\n            if (!seen[j]) {\n                sb += (char)('a' + j);\n                goto next_i;\n            }\n        }\n        next_i:;\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) sb += q;\n    return sb;\n}\n\nint countUniqueInRange(const string& pattern, int l, int r) {\n    vector<bool> seen(26, false);\n    int len = pattern.length();\n    if (r - l + 1 >= 100000) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n            seen[pattern[i] - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n    } else {\n        for (int i = l; i <= r; i++) {\n            seen[pattern[i % len] - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n    }\n    int count = 0;\n    for (bool b : seen) if (b) count++;\n    return count;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int a, b, l, r;\n    cin >> a >> b >> l >> r;\n    l--;\n    r--;\n    \n    int minUnique = 26;\n    \n    for (char p = 'a'; p <= 'z'; p++) {\n        for (char q = (char)('a' + a); q <= 'z'; q++) {\n            string pattern = buildPattern(a, b, p, q);\n            int uniqueCount = countUniqueInRange(pattern, l, r);\n            minUnique = min(minUnique, uniqueCount);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << minUnique << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00016473367577418685, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0018756669014692307, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.50339189733495e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.833439826965332, -2.861018856492592e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.057691872119903564, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0109320767223835, -6.627816765103489e-05, -0.0009116546134464443, -5.364403477869928e-06, -0.17273728549480438, -8.34461570775602e-06, -0.03364749997854233, -0.007811947725713253, -7.390948667307384e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.21864986419677734, -7.152